module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a reader that needs only the start of a text pays for the whole text. v2.compiler.tokenize tokenize_prefix_prepared stopped its WALK at a scalar limit, but its first step was `unicode_scalar_unfold(s: text)` over the WHOLE text, and v2.compiler.module_header module_header_read_window called it once per window attempt (the window starts at module_header_first_window and doubles until the header production settles). So the unfold was O(file) per attempt while the walk it fed was O(window): the prefix door made the lex proportional to the header and left the text ingress proportional to the file. A header that settled in the first window still unfolded every scalar of its file.",

    "REPAIRED, and what the repair had to carry. The window is now taken as a HOST substring (`substring(s: text, start: 0, end: n)`, truncation decided from a window one scalar wider) BEFORE the one declared crossing, so `unicode_scalar_unfold` converts the window and nothing past it. No new coercion plan is involved: the cut is host text to host text, and the crossing is the existing std.coercion route over a shorter String, so the section 4 ruling `text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold` is untouched and a knob on the unfold (one name, two contracts) was never needed. What a plain prefix cannot carry is the edge: a matcher that needs a scalar beyond the window of a truncated text must answer BEYOND, not no-match, or a token the edge falls inside is refused. The lexer therefore reads the text through a cursor whose head is one of three values (a scalar, the end of the text, beyond the window), Beyond dominates prefer-longer, the walk halts before consuming and reports the lex incomplete, and a windowed result is either Beyond or the whole lex's tokens (v2.test.claim.tokenize.lex_window_beyond, v2.test.claim.tokenize.lex_prefix_door, v2.test.claim.module_header).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. It is not the lex (the walk was windowed) and not the production (the tail is derived once per run by v2.compiler.grammar_reach grammar_production_tail). The unsound repair is the obvious one and it was measured: cutting the text at a scalar count and lexing the cut as if it were the file refuses modules the whole lex accepts. Cut at 4096 scalars, 14 modules refuse with tokenize_lex_e1_unrecognized_char, every one because the cut fell inside an open string literal (the closing quote is beyond the carrier, the string rule finds no match and the opening quote is an unrecognized character). Cut at 256, 133 refuse (132 e1_unrecognized_char and 1 e4_mode_unterminated at dag:gunbc/tools/cron_tag). Those refusals are the red control of the windowed repair, held as claims: a string literal, a template hole and an open mode straddling the first window's edge must not refuse the header, and the naive cut of the same text must (v2.test.claim.module_header a_string_literal_the_first_windows_edge_falls_inside_does_not_refuse_the_header).",

    "MEASURED by the live-roots extraction, one binary built from the emitted closure and three trees: the live roots (8335 modules, 107575909 bytes), a STUB TWIN with the same module names and paths in which each file holds only its `module` line (417864 bytes), and a one-file root; the verbs `check-layout` and `parse-population`, 2026-10-13, BEFORE = the tree of #13866 (whole-text unfold per attempt), AFTER = this change, built over main 0fb05cc2e3d and again over 17e2fd6a364 (the two builds). check-layout over the live roots: 37.97 s before, 6.76 to 6.83 s after (four runs on two builds of this change). check-layout over the stub twin: 3.30 to 3.40 s before, 3.35 s after (two builds). So the size-dependent term, live minus stub, fell from about 34.6 s to about 3.4 s. Arithmetic consistency, not an attribution: 107.6 million scalars at the 320 ns per scalar the interpreter's unfold costs is 34.4 s, which is the term that went. parse-population over the live roots: 490.7 s before, 487.5 and 499.8 s after (two builds, so the run-to-run spread exceeds any difference; stub twin 1.49 to 1.50 s after). That verb lexes and parses every module whole, so the windowed header cannot move it and it did not; it is not this class. The 3.4 s that remains over the stub twin is unattributed (reading and hashing 107 MB, and the first window's own unfold, about 0.7 s by the same arithmetic, are candidates; none is measured).",

    "MEASURED, the step it sits in, as the earlier receipt and a different instrument: the v2-native-cli step from `population controls - check-layout and parse-population over the live roots` to `live roots - check-layout held`. #13866 at adca9d6b (run 38378591395): 907.9 s. Six trees carrying #13842 without #13866: 1030.0 to 1137.6 s (median 1076). Two trees before #13842: 786.5 and 861.9 s. This row cites no step time for the repaired state; the repaired step is the witnesses run of the PR that lands this change, read with the same extraction of the step's two timestamps.",

    "HARM: DESIGN section 6, bare minimum cost: a proven cost-shape defect is always fixed regardless of realized n, because n is small here is not time-stable. Here n was every module of the live roots per verb, in a job that is one required context.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the cost was bounded by the file and the answer was correct). ATTAINABLE CEILING for THIS instance: the structural-text crossing is bounded by the window by construction, since the cut precedes the only crossing and a larger window is reached only by an incomplete lex. What stays file-proportional is host work at native cost (reading the file, hashing it, the carrier's ASCII flag), which is the unattributed 3.4 s above. The CLASS, a prefix consumer paying for its whole input, is a cost shape and stays a ratchet: it is observed by the extraction's live-minus-stub differential, not decided by a wall. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, the capability restored: the unfold producing its sequence at native per-scalar cost. The interpreter builds an im::Vector (v1_rt Vec) at about 320 to 400 ns per scalar (320 baseline, 398 residual in the unfold's microbenchmark, not retained), which every WHOLE-text lex still pays: by the arithmetic above about 34 s of parse-population's 487 s. It is restored when a flat scalar carrier backs List<Char> and the same extraction shows parse-population's live-minus-stub term fall by that amount. The windowed form needs no new coercion plan and is not waiting on this."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.tokenize", decl_name: "tokenize_prefix_prepared", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.tokenize", decl_name: "lex_window", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.module_header", decl_name: "module_header_read_window", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.coercion", decl_name: "unicode_scalar_unfold", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
